From 886f132f75675d810875b485d4e8d1c5d3aee351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:20:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VaapiEGL: the probe of the formats imports every layer as the
 import of a picture does, with the modifier of its layout

At start, CVaapi2Texture::TestInteropFormats() decides which VA formats
the EGL interop offers: NV12 decides whether Kodi has a VAAPI renderer at
all, P010 whether it takes 10-bit video (RendererVAAPIGLES::Register(),
RendererVAAPIGL::Register()). Its probe, TestEsh(), made attributes of
its own: of the first layer alone, without
EGL_DMA_BUF_PLANE0_MODIFIER_LO/HI_EXT, and without the layout that the
import gives packed 4:2:2 (ABGR16161616 at half width). Import() passed
the modifier wherever EGL takes modifiers. With a driver that exports a
layout other than linear (those of Intel and AMD can), the probe could fail where
the import of a picture works, and Kodi was left without its VAAPI
renderer, or without 10-bit video in it; or it could pass where the
import does not (a chroma layer that EGL refuses). Import() also passed
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID as a modifier, which is no layout but the
driver's word that it gives none.

One description of a layer is now made for both (DescribeLayer(),
ImportAttributes()): its DRM format, the size of its picture (the chroma
of 4:2:0 at half size, packed 4:2:2 at half width), its object, offset
and pitch, and the modifier of its object where EGL takes modifiers
(EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import_modifiers), DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR too.
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID is never passed: the buffer is imported with the
layout it has of its own. A layout with a modifier other than linear is
not imported where EGL takes no modifiers, as the bridge decides
(tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dmabuf.c, make_planes()): the probe says so in
kodi.log at WARNING and the format is not offered, the import says so at
ERROR. The probe tries every layer of the surface. The index of the
object of a layer is checked against the objects that the descriptor can
hold too, and the probe closes the descriptors of those alone.

The idea of probing with the exported modifier is CroqueMr's
(libreelec-x86-DV, preview/rc4-update3, d332f0799c, "Probe VAAPI EGL
surfaces with their exported DMA-BUF modifier"); written for this tree,
with one description of the layer for the probe and the import.
